Subject: [PATCH 6/6] [S] port deltas: register five labels in both
 completeness tables; bump guard pin

Port commit for the self-improvement loop onto experiment-5-frozen-r1.

Delta 3 [SHARED hunk]: the five S labels (TraceLabel, MotifLabel,
CompressedLawLabel, RefusedLabel, CandidateObservableLabel) register in both
labels.sync_from_namespace and persistence.SNAPSHOT_SYMBOL_NAMES. The
label_registration_completeness_test pins stay unchanged at 40 / 198 / 18:
registering keeps them put; the pins move only downward. The five are genuine
leaf ConstructorLabel singletons and transient markers (never persisted, never
in the provenance map), so the snapshot-table entries are benign
over-registration forced by the no-upward-pin rule.

Delta 4: TestShardCursorPinTest.EXPECTED_GUARD_COUNT 305 -> 310. Hard pin
(EXPECTED_CURSOR_INDEX 218, EXPECTED_SHARD 0) holds unchanged; registrations
land after every existing test.

Base: experiment-5-frozen-r1 (ef571b6). Port source commits (referenced by
hash, unaltered): 548c6f6 trace mining, 8738bcf rent gate, 1e45188 recursive
turn, 0e50bc1 invariant conjecture, 218a40f learned-memory cycle.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
